  (prompt/new/44.md, STEP 22 — "STEP 16" per the source's own internal
  numbering, which this repo does not follow; see ReplayProgress in
  index.md for the authoritative sequential count.) Source proposed a
  final "kernel" for the `.sdd/protocol/` directory floated at STEP 20
  and re-floated at STEP 21: 6 files (protocol.sdd [P1]-[P10], stages.sdd,
  states.sdd, relations.sdd [R1]-[R7], origins.sdd, vocabulary.sdd), a
  worked compact task-format example, and a token-economy statement
  ("AI should read the smallest sufficient context; AI must expand
  references only when required; human documentation should contain the
  full explanation; SDD should contain the compact operational model").

  Declined (third re-proposal of the same directory, same reasoning as
  STEP 20/21, this time with per-file verification against the concrete
  proposed content):
  - `protocol/stages.sdd` (AN/AR/DB/BE/API/FE/MD/QA/DO/VR) is a near-total
    subset of `chains/chains.sdd -> Stages:` (verified verbatim this
    STEP — same ten stage IDs, same orchestration/discipline split) —
    NoDuplication.
  - `protocol/states.sdd` (+ =READY, ~ =IN_PROGRESS, > =REVIEW, ? =BLOCKED,
    ! =FAILED, @ =HUMAN_ACTION) directly contradicts the canonical
    `state/state.sdd -> Symbols` (+ =DONE, ~ =ACTIVE, - =FAILED, ! =BLOCKED,
    ? =DECISION_REQUIRED, > =NEXT, @ =REFERENCE) — same symbols, different
    meanings, would violate `state.sdd`'s own `[S2]` ("state symbols MUST
    NOT be redefined by project components") and the proposal's own
    `[P2]`/`[P9]` rules against exactly this kind of collision.
  - `protocol/relations.sdd [R1]-[R7]` and `protocol/protocol.sdd
    [P1]-[P10]` would collide with this file's own root `Rules: [R1]-
    [R12]` and `prompts/prompts.sdd`'s own `[P1]-[P24]` — same rule-ID
    prefix, different authority, ambiguous for any future cross-reference.
  - `protocol/origins.sdd` — reaffirms the STEP 20 decline of a task
    `Origin` field; `tasks/tasks.sdd -> Source` (`[T18]`) already owns
    this concept, unchanged.
  - The standalone `protocol/` directory as a container is therefore
    declined a third time — every file it would hold either duplicates
    an existing owner or collides with an existing rule-ID range.
  - `vocabulary.sdd`'s `#TAG -> skill.md` mechanism — declined for now,
    same reasoning as STEP 20's skill-sigil decline: `skills/skills.sdd`
    is still catalog-only (STEP 6/18), no concrete skill file exists yet
    to tag.

  Applied: the token-economy statement was the one genuinely new item
  (STEP 21 had already confirmed, via grep, zero existing coverage of it
  anywhere in `.sdd/`). Added as two new named entries to
  `architecture/architecture.sdd -> Principles:` — `TokenEconomy` (AI
  MUST read the smallest sufficient context, MUST expand a reference only
  when the task requires it) and `CompactModel` (SDD content MUST stay
