  (prompt/new/45.md, STEP 23 — "STEP 17" in the source's own internal
  numbering, "Code ↔ SDD Mapping") Source proposed a concrete per-domain/
  per-component `.sdd/project/{domain}/{component}/map.sdd` directory
  tree with worked `@PAY/refund` examples, an `Owns:`/`Files:`/`Tests:`/
  `Entry:`/`Dependencies:`/`DependsOn:`/`UsedBy:`/`Triggers:`/`Produces:`
  field schema, a `SourceTruth` table, a MAP DRIFT concept with new
  `!MAP_MISMATCH`/`!DRIFT` symbols, a hierarchical semantic-ID navigation
  tree (`@PROJECT -> @PAY -> @REFUND`), and a human-doc-vs-AI-doc routing
  table. Each item evaluated on its own merits:

  Declined: the concrete directory tree and `@PAY/refund` worked
  examples — no real domain directories exist yet (same precedent as
  STEP 4's "Tam sıfırla" and the three-time decline of `protocol/` across
  STEP 20/21/22). Declined: the hierarchical semantic-ID navigation tree
  — duplicates the existing `map.sdd -> Resolution[module|domain|
  feature]` mechanism (NoDuplication). Declined: the human-doc vs AI-doc
  routing table — `architecture.sdd -> Principles -> CompactModel`
  already states this exact split ("rules, not prose... full narrative
  belongs to human-facing documentation"), a second table would itself
  violate NoDuplication.

  Applied to `project/map.sdd -> Rules:`: a three-rule principle — AI
  MUST NOT trust a resolved map entry blindly (the map returns a
  pointer, not the fact itself), AI MUST use the map only to navigate,
  and source code/tests/the DB-API contract are what confirm the fact.
  Applied to `project/map.sdd -> CodeReference:`: a `SourceOfTruth:`
  subsection (an abstract table — runtime behavior/data shape/contract
  -> source code, test correctness -> tests, project organization ->
  the project model, engineering rule -> architecture.sdd, execution
  order -> chains.sdd; no concrete domain example, since none exists
  yet) and a `Drift:` subsection — MAP DRIFT is kept as a concept, but
  routed through the existing `!` (BLOCKED) state symbol with a
  descriptive `reason: map-drift` (bax state.sdd `[S2]`/`[S7]`) and
  escalated to a task (bax tasks.sdd -> Source), rather than inventing
  the source's proposed new symbols — a new symbol would collide with
  the canonical `state.sdd -> Symbols` list, the same reasoning STEP 22
  used to decline a parallel `protocol/states.sdd`.

  Applied to `project/modules.sdd -> Rules:`: optional `files` (owned
  source paths) and `entry` (primary entry-point file) fields, plus
  `tests` (owned test paths) — all routing pointers only, cross-
  referencing `map.sdd -> CodeReference -> SourceOfTruth`. Declined
  (modules.sdd): `Owns:`/`Dependencies:`/`DependsOn:` — already present
  in modules.sdd's own Rules (NoDuplication). Declined: `UsedBy:` —
  derivable as the reverse of `deps`, a separate field would itself be
  a duplicate-risk source of truth. Declined: `Triggers:`/`Produces:` —
  execution/event concepts already owned by chains.sdd/tasks.sdd,
  premature and duplicate here.

  Function-level mapping's optionality required no separate addition —
  already covered by `architecture.sdd -> Principles ->
  TokenEconomy/CompactModel` (bax STEP 22). No new rule-ID prefix was
  needed; all changes landed inside the existing `project/map.sdd ->
  Rules:`/`CodeReference:` and `project/modules.sdd -> Rules:` sections.
  See `project/map.sdd -> Note` and `project/modules.sdd -> Note` for
  the mirrored entries.
